  "details": "It would be cool to add support for vibration of the vive trackers in vrchat.\nYou can drive a vibration motor using the pogo pins on the vive tracker quite easily.\nIt would be low cost haptics feedback for full body users.\nCoding it would be really simple as there are plenty of examples and documentation for this within unity\nThe tracker straps with build in battery bank can be used to power a vibration motor on the back side (to not shake your trackers) with the vive tracker driving the signal upon object collission or event trigger.",
